A weather team adds two same-size tables a and b into c with:
for (int r = 0; r < c.length; r++) {
  for (int col = 0; col < c[0].length; col++) {
    ______;
  }
}
Which blank fills c correctly?

A score table holds 2 rows and 3 columns in int[][] grid. A printer runs:
for (int r = 0; r < 2; r++) {
  for (int c = 0; c < 3; c++) {
    System.out.print(grid[c][r] + " ");
  }
}
It crashes with ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException. Which choice best describes the bug?

A coach finds the best score in row 0 of int[][] pts = {{4, 9, 2}, {7, 1, 5}}; with:
int best = pts[0][0];
for (int c = 1; c < pts[0].length; c++) {
  if (pts[0][c] > best) {
    best = pts[0][c];
  }
}
What does best hold afterward?

A harvest table holds int[][] crop = {{5, 1, 8}, {3, 9, 2}}; A scan finds the largest value in column 1:
int best = crop[0][1];
for (int r = 1; r < crop.length; r++) {
  if (crop[r][1] > best) {
    best = crop[r][1];
  }
}
What does best hold afterward?

A quilt program totals the main diagonal of a square int[][] grid with:
int total = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < grid.length; i++) {
  total += ______;
}
Which blank adds the diagonal?

A ledger holds 3 rows and 2 columns in int[][] ledger. A totaling loop runs:
for (int r = 0; r < ledger.length; r++) {
  for (int c = 0; c < ledger.length; c++) {
    total += ledger[r][c];
  }
}
It crashes reaching for column 2. Which fix is correct?

A photo method should return a doubled copy while leaving the input grid alone, but it starts with:
int[][] doubled = original;
for (int r = 0; r < doubled.length; r++) {
  for (int c = 0; c < doubled[r].length; c++) {
    doubled[r][c] = original[r][c] * 2;
  }
}
Callers find their grid changed. Which choice best describes the bug?

An usher searches String[][] hall for a guest named Jo with:
String target = "Jo";
int foundRow = -1;
int foundCol = -1;
for (int r = 0; r < hall.length; r++) {
  for (int c = 0; c < hall[r].length; c++) {
    if (______) {
      foundRow = r;
      foundCol = c;
    }
  }
}
Which blank finds the guest?

A banquet chart holds String[][] hall = {{"Jo", "Kim", "Lee"}, {"Pat", "Jo", "Ari"}}; and a loop counts cells equal to "Jo":
int count = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < hall.length; r++) {
  for (int c = 0; c < hall[r].length; c++) {
    if (hall[r][c].equals("Jo")) {
      count++;
    }
  }
}
What does count hold?

A jagged score table holds int[][] grid = {{1, 2, 3}, {4}, {5, 6}}; A totaling loop runs:
int total = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
  for (int c = 0; c < grid[0].length; c++) {
    total += grid[r][c];
  }
}
It crashes on the short row. Which choice best describes the flaw?
